                                            <li data-content="creatives" class="" id="creatives">
                            <div class="o-grid o-grid--flush o-grid--center">
                                <div class="o-grid__cell u-1/1@desktop">
    <div class="c-col c-col-biographies c-col c-col-biographies u-transparent-bg c-col-biographies-grid">

                    <div class="c-wysiwyg c-col-titles">
                <p>Creatives</p>
            </div>
        
                    <div class="c-biographies-container o-grid o-grid--center">
                                                        <div class="o-grid__cell">
                        <div class="c-single-bio c-single-bio--link">
                                                            <a class="c-single-bio__link" href="#" data-modal-open="bio--6adca74f7539a" role="button" tabindex="0">
                                    <span class="u-hidden-visually">Clifford Odets</span>
                                </a>
                                                                                                                    <h5 class="c-col-title">Clifford Odets</h5>
                            
                                                            <p class="c-col-subtitle">Writer</p>
                            
                                                            <div id="bio--6adca74f7539a" hidden class="c-modal c-modal--biography" data-modal data-modal-close="Close" data-modal-close-class="c-modal__close-btn" data-modal-close-focus>
                                    <div data-modal-document>
                                        <div class="c-modal__wrap">
                                            <div class="c-modal__header"></div>

                                            <div class="c-modal__content c-modal__content--bio">
                                                <div class="o-grid">
                                                                                                        <div class="o-grid__cell u-2/3@desktop">
                                                        <h2 class="c-col-title">Clifford Odets</h2>
                                                        <div class="c-single-bio__excerpt c-wysiwyg">
                                                            <p>Clifford Odets began his career in 1931 as an actor and then playwright for New York’s the Group Theatre. His first play for the Group, <em>Waiting for Lefty</em> (1935), immediately launched him as the most celebrated American playwright of the 1930s. Five major Broadway productions of his plays followed in that decade and introduced theatre audiences to subject matter and language that had never before been heard on the American stage. This work deeply influenced generations of American playwrights to follow. Odets’ other best-known plays include <em>Awake and Sing!</em>;<em> Paradise Lost</em>; <em>Golden Boy</em>; <em>Rocket to the Moon</em>; <em>Clash by Night</em>; <em>The Big </em><em>Knife and The Flowering Peach</em>. Screenplay credits include <em>None but the Lonely Heart</em>; <em>Humoresque</em>; <em>Sweet Smell of </em><em>Success and The Story on Page One</em>. He also directed both <em>None but the Lonely Heart </em>and <em>The Story on Page One</em>. Alongside <em>Golden Boy</em>, two more of Odets’ greatest plays will be revived later this year: <em>Waiting for Lefty</em> will be produced in New York by the Classic Stage Company and <em>Awake and Sing!</em> will be presented on Broadway at the Manhattan Theatre Club.</p>
                                                        </div>
                                                    </div>
                                                </div>
                                            </div>
                                        </div>
                                    </div>
                                </div>
                            

                        </div>
                    </div>
                                                        <div class="o-grid__cell">
                        <div class="c-single-bio c-single-bio--link">
                                                            <a class="c-single-bio__link" href="#" data-modal-open="bio--6adca74f757b0" role="button" tabindex="0">
                                    <span class="u-hidden-visually">Sam Yates</span>
                                </a>
                                                                                                                    <h5 class="c-col-title">Sam Yates</h5>
                            
                                                            <p class="c-col-subtitle">Director</p>
                            
                                                            <div id="bio--6adca74f757b0" hidden class="c-modal c-modal--biography" data-modal data-modal-close="Close" data-modal-close-class="c-modal__close-btn" data-modal-close-focus>
                                    <div data-modal-document>
                                        <div class="c-modal__wrap">
                                            <div class="c-modal__header"></div>

                                            <div class="c-modal__content c-modal__content--bio">
                                                <div class="o-grid">
                                                                                                        <div class="o-grid__cell u-2/3@desktop">
                                                        <h2 class="c-col-title">Sam Yates</h2>
                                                        <div class="c-single-bio__excerpt c-wysiwyg">
                                                            <p>Sam is an Olivier Award-winning director and producer working in theatre, film and television.</p>
<p><strong>Theatre includes:</strong> <em>VANYA</em> (West End/ Broadway, Olivier and WhatsOnStage Awards for Best Revival, Outer Critics’ Circle and Drama League Awards for Outstanding Revival of a Play and Lucille Lortel Award for Outstanding Solo Show); <em>The Two Character Play</em> (Hampstead Theatre); <em>Incantata</em> (Galway Arts Festival/ Gate Theatre, Dublin/ Irish Repertory Theatre, New York); <em>The Phlebotomist </em>(Hampstead Theatre, Olivier Award nomination for Outstanding Achievement in an Affiliate Theatre);<em> The </em><em>Starry Messenger</em>; <em>Murder Ballad</em> (West End); <em>Glengarry </em><em>Glen Ross</em>; <em>East is East</em> (West End/ UK tour); <em>Desire Under </em><em>the Elms</em> (Sheffield Theatres); <em>Cymbeline</em> (Shakespeare’s Globe); <em>Outside Mullingar</em> (Theatre Royal Bath);<em> Billy Liar </em>(Royal Exchange Theatre, Manchester); <em>The El Train</em> (Hoxton Hall); <em>Cornelius</em> (Finborough Theatre/ 59E59 Theaters, New York), <em>Mixed Marriage</em> (Finborough Theatre).</p>
<p><strong>Film includes:</strong> <em>Magpie</em>; <em>VANYA</em> (National Theatre Live); <em>The </em><em>Hope Rooms</em>.</p>
<p><strong>Television includes:</strong> <em>Towards Zero</em>; <em>Agatha and the Curse </em><em>of Ishtar</em>.</p>
                                                        </div>
                                                    </div>
                                                </div>
                                            </div>
                                        </div>
                                    </div>
                                </div>
                            

                        </div>
                    </div>
                                                        <div class="o-grid__cell">
                        <div class="c-single-bio c-single-bio--link">
