                                </a>
                                                                                                                    <h5 class="c-col-title">Isobel Waller-Bridge</h5>
                            
                                                            <p class="c-col-subtitle">Composer & Arranger</p>
                            
                                                            <div id="bio--6adca74f7687f" hidden class="c-modal c-modal--biography" data-modal data-modal-close="Close" data-modal-close-class="c-modal__close-btn" data-modal-close-focus>
                                    <div data-modal-document>
                                        <div class="c-modal__wrap">
                                            <div class="c-modal__header"></div>

                                            <div class="c-modal__content c-modal__content--bio">
                                                <div class="o-grid">
                                                                                                        <div class="o-grid__cell u-2/3@desktop">
                                                        <h2 class="c-col-title">Isobel Waller-Bridge</h2>
                                                        <div class="c-single-bio__excerpt c-wysiwyg">
                                                            <p>Isobel is an award-winning composer known for her scores for film, television, ballet, and theatre, alongside her work in electronic and contemporary classical music. She works in a wide range of genres, extending across large-scale orchestral music, electronic sound design, experimental music, and songwriting. Isobel’s album releases include her 2025 album <em>Objects,</em> her 2022 album <em>VIII</em> in collaboration with 12 Ensemble, singles <em>Illuminations</em> and <em>September,</em> and 2015’s<em> Music for Strings</em>.</p>
<p><strong>Theatre includes:</strong> <em>The House of Bernada Alba</em>; <em>The Unknown</em> (National Theatre).</p>
<p><strong>Film includes:</strong> <em>Munich: The Edge of War</em>; <em>Emma</em>; <em>I Came By</em>; <em>Wicked Little Letters</em>; <em>The Lesson</em>; <em>Magpie</em>; <em>The Boy, the Mole, the Fox, and the Horse</em>; <em>Siren</em>.</p>
<p><strong>Television includes:</strong> <em>Fleabag</em>; <em>Black Mirror</em>;<em> Three Women</em>; <em>Sweetpea</em>.</p>
<p><strong>Dance includes:</strong> <em>Crime and Punishment</em> (American Ballet Theatre); <em>Entress</em> (Scottish Ballet).</p>
<p><strong>Other work includes:</strong> <em>Temperatures</em> (Royal Festival Hall); <em>Dreamland Sirens</em> (Frieze London); <em>Salt of the Earth</em> (Venice Biennale); <em>Hermès</em>;<em> Alexander McQueen</em>; <em>Simone Rocha</em>.</p>
                                                        </div>
                                                    </div>
                                                </div>
                                            </div>
                                        </div>
                                    </div>
                                </div>
                            

                        </div>
                    </div>
