                                                        <h2 class="c-col-title">Jim Carnahan CSA</h2>
                                                        <div class="c-single-bio__excerpt c-wysiwyg">
                                                            <p>Jim has cast over 185 Broadway shows. He is a member of the Casting Society of America and a 26-time recipient of the Artios Award for Excellence in Casting.</p>
<p><strong>Theatre includes:</strong> <em>Fallen Angels</em>; <em>Oedipus</em>; <em>Chess</em>; <em>Waiting for Godot</em>; <em>ART</em>; <em>Just in Time</em>; <em>Pirates! The Penzance Musical</em>; <em>Sunset Blvd.</em>; <em>The Hills of California</em>; <em>Appropriate</em>; <em>Merrily We Roll Along</em>; <em>A Doll’s House</em>; <em>A Beautiful Noise</em>; <em>Leopoldstadt</em>; <em>Funny Girl</em>; <em>Take Me Out</em>;<em> The Lehman Trilogy</em>; <em>Moulin Rouge! The Musical</em>; <em>The Ferryman</em>; <em>Harry Potter and the Cursed Child</em>;<em> Fun Home</em>; <em>Cabaret</em>; <em>Matilda The Musical</em>; <em>Once</em>; <em>Boeing-Boeing</em>; <em>Spring Awakening</em> (Broadway); <em>Stranger Things: The First Shadow</em> (West End/ Broadway); <em>Copenhagen</em>; <em>The Assembled Parties</em> (Hampstead Theatre); <em>Romeo &amp; Juliet</em>;<em> Woman in Mind</em>; <em>Evita</em>; <em>Enemy of the People</em>; <em>Best of Enemies</em>; <em>Plaza Suite</em> (West End); <em>The Seagull</em> (Barbican); <em>Oedipus</em>; <em>Eureka Day</em> (The Old Vic).</p>
<p><strong>Film includes:</strong> <em>Beau Is Afraid</em>; <em>The Seagull</em>; <em>John Mulaney &amp; the Sack Lunch Bunch</em>; <em>A Home at the End of the World</em>; <em>Flicka</em>.</p>
<p><strong>Television includes:</strong> <em>Glee</em> (Emmy nomination for Outstanding Casting for a Comedy Series).</p>
                                                        </div>
