                                                                                                        <div class="o-grid__cell u-2/3@desktop">
                                                        <h2 class="c-col-title">Yasmin Hafesji</h2>
                                                        <div class="c-single-bio__excerpt c-wysiwyg">
                                                            <p>Yasmin studied at the University of Cambridge and trained with the Young Vic and National Theatre Studio. She is Deputy Artistic Director at Theatre503 and was Associate Director at the Gate Theatre from 2020–2022.</p>
<p><strong>For the Almeida:</strong></p>
<p><strong>As Director:</strong> <em>The Maladies</em> (Almeida Young Company).</p>
<p><strong>As Assistant Director:</strong> <em>The Years</em>; <em>The Tragedy of Macbeth</em>.</p>
<p><strong>Theatre includes:</strong></p>
<p><strong>As Director:</strong> <em>Swallow the Lake</em> (Mercury Theatre, Colchester); <em>A Sudden Violent Burst of Rain</em>; <em>Two Heads and a Hand</em>; <em>The Jokers</em> (Gate Theatre); <em>The Sex Ed Musical</em> (UK tour); <em>Electra</em> (Royal Central School of Speech and Drama); <em>Kick</em> (Lyric Hammersmith, The Bill Cashmore Award); <em>Fresh Direction: Replay</em> (Young Vic); <em>Watch Me Dance!</em>; <em>Young Writers Group Showcase</em> (Bush Theatre).</p>
<p><strong>As Assistant Director/ Associate Director:</strong><em> London Tide</em>; <em>The Motive and the Cue</em> (National Theatre); <em>Women Beware Women</em> (Shakespeare’s Globe); <em>Fairview</em> (Young Vic); <em>Dear Elizabeth</em> (Gate Theatre).</p>
                                                        </div>
